    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In this paper, we do not study the question of EA-equivalence of the (2m, t)-bent functions deﬁned above. In general, this is a very diﬃcult question. We only remark that Weng, Feng and Qui [23] proved that most of the PS type bent functions, obtained from a Desarguesian spread are not EA-equivalent to any Maiorana–McFarland bent function. This leads us to conclude that, typically, for t > 1, the (2m, t)-bent functions described by (9) are generally not EA-equivalent to the other two classes, as speciﬁed in (6) and (8)."
  }, {
