    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 56.639, 177.099, 538.679, 232.278 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof of Theorem 1. Let Ei be the set of pairs (x, y) ∈ GF(2m)2 such that fi(x, y) = fi(0, 0), i = 1, 2. We show that |Ei| = 22m−t + 2m − 2m−t, which implies that fi has Hamming distance (1−2−t)(22m −2m) from the constant function fi(0, 0). Therefore, dH(fi, A) ≤ (1−2−t)(22m − 2m), and the theorem follows from the Carlet-Ding-Yuan bound."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 36,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 56.639, 110.063, 538.614, 176.478 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Let T be the set of elements z ∈ GF(qm) with γ(z) = f1(0, 0). Since γ is balanced, |T| = 2m−t, and f1(x, y) = f1(0, 0) if and only if ⋆xy ∈ T. Moreover, since ⋆00 = 0, we have 0 ∈ T. The number of solutions of ⋆xy = 0 is 2 · 2m − 1, and the number of solutions of ⋆xy = t ∈ T \\ {0} is 2m − 1. This implies"
  }, {
